Lets ANGLE build for macOS 11.0, Limn's floor (limn-toolkit's OsFloors): kIOMainPortDefault was
introduced in macOS 12.0, and ANGLE's build treats its unguarded use as an error once the deployment
target is 11.0. The constant's value is MACH_PORT_NULL, which IOKit takes as the default main port
on every version, so the call is the same on 12 and later and also links on 11. The four uses are
the only availability errors a macOS 11.0 build of this commit has (a build with warnings not fatal
listed every one).

diff --git a/src/common/apple_platform_utils.mm b/src/common/apple_platform_utils.mm
index 635abb6..e31d759 100644
--- a/src/common/apple_platform_utils.mm
+++ b/src/common/apple_platform_utils.mm
@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@ bool IsMetalRendererAvailable()
 bool GetMacosMachineModel(std::string *outMachineModel)
 {
     io_service_t platformExpert = IOServiceGetMatchingService(
-        kIOMainPortDefault, IOServiceMatching("IOPlatformExpertDevice"));
+        MACH_PORT_NULL, IOServiceMatching("IOPlatformExpertDevice"));
 
     if (platformExpert == IO_OBJECT_NULL)
     {
